    text:"Amazon announced it will shut down Mechanical Turk, the crowdsourced human-task marketplace Jeff Bezos once called \"artificial artificial intelligence,\" on September 30, 2026, after 21 years. The platform peaked at more than 500,000 workers completing small digital tasks like data labeling and transcription; Amazon stopped accepting new customers last month, and a wave of newer data-labeling startups (Scale AI, Mercor, Prolific) has drawn workers away as AI training-data demand shifted.",
    why:"The service Amazon itself once marketed as a joke about AI being humans-in-disguise is closing just as real AI training-data labeling has become a multi-billion-dollar industry run by companies MTurk's own decline helped create room for.",
