    text:"Anthropic committed $45 billion to Nscale, a British AI infrastructure company, for compute over six years, bringing approximately 460 megawatts of power capacity from Nscale's West Virginia data center online by late 2027. The deal sources compute via Nvidia's Vera Rubin chips. Nscale, founded in 2024, has already cut deals with Microsoft; Anthropic has announced over $100 billion in similar compute commitments this year across multiple vendors including Fluidstack, Volta Infra, and SpaceX.",
