    text:"Hugging Face and Pollen Robotics opened pre-orders for Microduck, a $399 open-source biped robot: 25cm tall, under 800g, 15 motors, a camera and small LiDAR, that can waddle, pick things up with its beak, fall and get back up, and even roller-skate. Its SDK, MuJoCo simulation environment and reinforcement-learning training stack are all released under an Apache 2.0 license; CEO Clem Delangue called it 'an open-source robot you can teach new tricks with reinforcement learning.'",
